# warnings

## UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE

```text
[UNSUPPORTED_FEATURE] `import defer` is currently lowered to a normal import, because `preserveModules` is on and a static import cycle can access the deferred namespace in `main.js` before its runtime helpers load. This changes execution timing because side effects run immediately instead of when the deferred import is first used. `experimental.importDefer` does not keep the deferred evaluation in this build yet.
   ╭─[ main.js:1:1 ]
   │
 1 │ import defer * as ns from './target.js';
   │ ────────────────────┬───────────────────  
   │                     ╰───────────────────── The deferred phase is removed here.
───╯

```

